{ Lets continue with the first opening. The London System. To play the London, play d4 🙂 }
1. d4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] d4 is a smart alternative to the more widely played e4. } (1. c4 e5 2. g3 d5 (2... Ne7)) 1... d5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Follow my arrows to learn the London! } { [%csl Gf4][%cal Gc1f4] } 2. Bf4 Nf6 { [%csl Ge3][%cal Ge2e3] } 3. e3 e6 { Now? } { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gg1f3] } 4. Nf3 Bd6 { [%anno "dUbEaR504", dubear504] Play, Ne5. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gf3e5] } 5. Ne5 (5. Bg3?! c5 6. Nbd2 Qc7 { [%cal Gc7e5,Ge6e5] } 7. c3 Nbd7 $132 { [%anno "dUbEaR504", dubear504] Now Black has some counterplay. } { [%cal Ge6e5,Gb7b6,Gc8b7,Gf6e4] } (7... Nc6? 8. dxc5 { [%cal Gg3c7,Gd6c5] })) 5... c5 { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gc2c3] } 6. c3 { [%anno "dUbEaR504", dubear504] Now you've made a pyramid! } { [%csl Gb2,Gc3,Gd4,Ge3,Gf2] } 6... Qc7 { [%csl Gd2][%cal Gb1d2] } 7. Nd2 Nbd7 { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gd2f3] } 8. Ndf3 Ne4 { [%csl Gd3][%cal Gf1d3] } 9. Bd3 O-O { [%anno "dUbEaR504", dubear504] Castle. } { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ge1g1] } 10. O-O f6 { [%anno "dUbEaR504", dubear504] Black kicks the knight. Take the knight. } { [%csl Gd7][%cal Ge5d7] } 11. Nxd7 Bxd7 { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gd3e4] } 12. Bxe4 dxe4 { [%csl Gd6][%cal Gf4d6] } 13. Bxd6 Qxd6 { [%csl Gc5][%cal Gd4c5] } 14. dxc5 Qxd1 { [%csl Gd1][%cal Gf1d1] } 15. Rfxd1 $16 { [%anno "dUbEaR504", dubear504] White's up a pawn. } { [%cal Gd1d7,Ge4f3] } *


