{ The Vienna is a good opening that you can play tactically or Gambit-style. It is IM Levy's favorite as White. To play this opening, first you have to play e4🙂 }
1. e4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] e4 is the most played move in the world (I feel like i have told that before). } 1... e5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Black copies us to increase strength on the center. Now black will be hoping that white plays Nf3 into his comfort zone. But we don't do that. PLAY NC3! } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gb1c3] } 2. Nc3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] White's wish is that to remove the e5 pawn with f4 and strengthen the center. } 2... Nf6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Black camouflages our control on d5 now, there are multiple options now. But let's play the most common one. } { [%anno "VofDoom41", vofdoom41] f4 } { [%csl Gf4][%cal Gf2f4] } 3. f4!! { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] BAM. White sacrifices the pawn on f4 to gain control over the center. Lets see if black takes it. } 3... d5! { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] BLACK OFFERS A GAMBIT OF HIS OWN! This move is very good by black. Lets see what do we do now. It is obvious, isn't it? } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gf4e5] } 4. fxe5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] We take the pawn with our weakest pawn. Black will always play Nxe4. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gf6e4] } 4... Nxe4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] here we have a Variety of options. Let's go with the most common one. } { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gg1f3] } 5. Nf3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Follow my arrows to learn the Vienna. } { [%anno "VofDoom41", vofdoom41] t } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Ge4c3] } 5... Nxc3 { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gd2c3] } 6. dxc3 { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gd2c3] } 6... Be6 { [%csl Ge6,Gd3][%cal Gc8e6,Gf1d3] } 7. Bd3 Bc5 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gf3d4] } 8. Nd4 Bxd4 9. cxd4 O-O { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ge1g1] } 10. O-O *


