{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] The Giuoco Piano is an Variation of the Italian opening that can be used against 3. Bc4. Do you remember the first moves? }
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 { Now? } 3. Bc4 Bc5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the Giuoco Piano that black can use to counter the 3. Bc4 move by white. Just follow the arrows to learn how to play this variation! } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gc2c3] } 4. c3 Nf6 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd2d4] } 5. d4 exd4 { Now? } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc3d4] } 6. cxd4 Bb4+ { Block! } { [%csl Gd2][%cal Gc1d2] } 7. Bd2 Bxd2+ { [%csl Gd2][%cal Gb1d2] } (7... Nxe4? 8. Bxb4 Nxb4 9. O-O O-O) 8. Nbxd2 O-O { Castle. } { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ge1g1] } 9. O-O { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] You now have a Great position. } { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] You now have played the Giuoco Piano version of the Italian opening. And also are in a great position to play. } (9. d5 { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] This is actually best. } { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] d5 and O-O are both good moves. } 9... Ne7) *


