{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Do you remember the first moves of the Ruy Lopez? }
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 { Now? } 3. Bb5 a6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Black defends the attack on the knight on c6 by pushing a6. Try to keep the bishop on the diagonal. } { [%csl Ga4][%cal Gb5a4] } 4. Ba4 Nf6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Follow the Arrows to learn how to play the Morphy Defense. Also do not worry about the pawn. If black is smart, he wont take the pawn. } { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ge1g1] } 5. O-O Be7 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Bring the Rook to e1 } { [%csl Ge1][%cal Gf1e1] } 6. Re1 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the Mainline of how to play the Morphy Defense. In the next chapter we will use the Marshall attack. } 6... b5 { [%csl Gb3][%cal Ga4b3] } 7. Bb3 O-O { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gc2c3] } 8. c3 Na5 { Retreat the Bishop. } { [%csl Gc2][%cal Gb3c2] } 9. Bc2 c5 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd2d4] } 10. d4 cxd4 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc3d4] } 11. cxd4 exd4 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gf3d4] } 12. Nxd4 { [%cal Gc1f4,Ge4e5,Gb1c3,Ga1c1] } *


