[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] The Marshall Attack is an attack used by black to pressure white's center. Now we will know how to counter this attack. Do you remember the first moves of the Ruy Lopez: Morphy Defense? }
1. e4 e5 { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gg1f3] } 2. Nf3 Nc6 { Now? } { [%csl Gb5][%cal Gf1b5] } 3. Bb5 a6 { And now? } { [%csl Ga4][%cal Gb5a4] } 4. Ba4 Nf6 { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ge1g1] } 5. O-O Be7 { Put the rook on e1. } { [%csl Ge1][%cal Gf1e1] } 6. Re1 { [%csl Gb7] } 6... b5 { [%csl Gb3][%cal Ga4b3] } 7. Bb3 O-O { Now? } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gc2c3] } 8. c3 d5!! { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] BAM. Black goes on a all-out attack with d5. Do not panic against this move. I will tell you how to counter this attack. Play exd5 } { [%csl Gd5][%cal Ge4d5] } 9. exd5 Nxd5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Take the pawn with Nxe5 } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gf3e5] } 10. Nxe5 Nxe5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] take the knight with Rxe5 } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Ge1e5] } 11. Rxe5 Nf6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Retreat the Rook with Re1. } 12. Re1 Bd6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Play h3 to prevent the attack on the queen } { [%csl Gh3][%cal Gh2h3] } 13. h3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Now this is the way to counter the aggressive Marshall Attack. } 13... Bb7 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gd2d4] } 14. d4 Qd7 { [%csl Ge3][%cal Gc1e3] } 15. Be3 { White is up a pawn. } *


