{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Do you remember the first moves? }
1. e4 e6 2. d4 { Now? } 2... d5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] We are here again at this moment. White takes the pawn with exd5 } 3. exd5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Play exd5 } { [%csl Gd5][%cal Ge6d5] } 3... exd5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the French Defense's Exchange Variation } 4. Nf3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Nf3 gains development in the center. Play Nf6 to copy them } { [%csl Gf6][%cal Gg8f6] } 4... Nf6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Now just follow my arrows to find out about the French Defense! } 5. Bd3 { [%csl Gd6][%cal Gf8d6] } 5... Bd6 6. O-O { [%csl Gg8][%cal Ge8g8] } 6... O-O { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the French Defense Exchange Variation piece setup of the black pieces.
Stockfish says +0.1 } *


