{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Another variation of the French Defense. Do you remember the first moves? }
1. e4 e6 2. d4 { Now? } 2... d5 3. e5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Here white advanced with the pawn instead of taking with the pawn. Now you have to move the c pawn to c5. } 3... c5 4. c3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Here white plays c3, trying to defend the pawn. Now just follow our arrows to learn the advanced variation of the French Defense! } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gb8c6] } 4... Nc6 { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gg1f3] } 5. Nf3 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc5d4] } 5... cxd4 { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc5d4] } 6. cxd4 { Follow my arrows to Learn the French! } { [%csl Gb4][%cal Gf8b4] } 6... Bb4+ { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is also known as the Paulsen Attack } 7. Bd2 { [%csl Gb6][%cal Gd8b6] } 7... Qb6! { [%csl Gb6][%cal Gd8b6] } (7... Qc7) 8. Bxb4! { Now? } { [%csl Gb4][%cal Gb6b4] } (8. Bc3! Nge7 9. Bd3 Ng6 10. O-O O-O { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] With okay position. }) 8... Qxb4+ 9. Nc3 { And Now? } { [%csl Gb2][%cal Gb4b2] } 9... Qxb2 10. Rc1? { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] You are up a pawn. } { [%csl Ge7][%cal Gg8e7] } (10. Nb5! { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] This is a tricky move. } { [%csl Gb4][%cal Gb2b4] } 10... Qb4+ { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] Only move. } 11. Nd2 { [%csl Ga5] } (11. Qd2 Qxd2+ 12. Kxd2 Kd8) 11... Qxb5 { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] not this } (11... Qa5 { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] this } 12. Nd6+ Kf8 { [%anno "Toadddddddd", toadddddddd] you are fine. })) 10... Nge7 *


