{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Do you remember the first moves? }
1. e4 c5! { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Black plays Nf3 to fortify the center. } 2. Nf3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Here you can go Nc6 to play the Old Sicillian, but we are Modern People, we check out recent stuff. Play d6 } 2... d6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] this move gets a nice little chain of pawns in the center. Lets see what white does now. } 3. d4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Ah, here we go again. Threatening the pawn on c5 with the d pawn. Not to worry. play cxd5. } { [%csl Gd4][%cal Gc5d4] } 3... cxd4 4. Nxd4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] White takes back with the knight. Play Nf6 now. } 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] black defends the pawn with Nc3. Play a6. } { [%csl Ga6][%cal Ga7a6] } 5... a6 $14 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the Najdorf Variation of the Sicillian Defense. This move stops the attack on the queen by Bb5 and removing the key square on b5. } *


