{ [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] The King's Indian Defense is also one of the most famous openings used by the Grandmasters. Hikaru Nakamura used this opening to win some matches. Let's see how to play this opening. }
1. d4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] White plays d4. Now play Nf6 } { [%csl Gf6][%cal Gg8f6] } 1... Nf6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] The Knight is used to stop the e pawn from moving and prevents the d pawn to advance. } 2. c4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] White increases control over the center with c4. Play g6 } 2... g6 3. Nc3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] White play Nc3 to put the knight behind a wall of pawns. Fianchetto the bishop. } 3... Bg7 4. e4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] White plays e4 to attack the knight with e5. To stop that attack, play d6 } { [%csl Gd6][%cal Gd7d6] } 4... d6 5. Nf3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Now what should you do? } 5... O-O { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] this is the King's Indian defense. With the move d6 Black opens the bishop. White gets a big center, but do not fear, we can bring it back. } *


