{ Now, The Dutch Defense. It is rarely played nowadays, but that does not mean that this opening is bad. White has to play d4 to let us play the Dutch. }
1. d4 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] We do not play the Orthodox lines like Nf6 or d5. We play f5. } 1... f5 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the Dutch Defense and this move stops e4. White normally plays g3. } 2. g3 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Here black needs to play Nf6. } { [%csl Gf6][%cal Gg8f6] } 2... Nf6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] Follow the Arrows to learn the Dutch. } 3. Bg2 { [%csl Gg6][%cal Gg7g6] } 3... g6 { [%csl Gg1,Gf3][%cal Gg1f3] } (3... e6 { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This move is also good. }) 4. Nf3 { Now? } { [%csl Gg7][%cal Gf8g7] } 4... Bg7 5. O-O { And Now? } { [%csl Gg8][%cal Ge8g8] } 5... O-O { [%anno "ArjunShukla23", arjunshukla23] This is the Dutch Defense: Semi-Leningrad. } *


